# Example ReRDMFT input file: water, STO-3G, MULLER (JK-only) functional, with JK_FROZEN_PAIRS
# and JK_ACTIVE_PAIRS -- restricts the fractional-occupation SQP to a small active window instead
# of letting every spin-orbital compete for occupation (compare water_muller.inp, same system with
# neither keyword set).
#
# NON_REL has 14 spin-orbitals (7 spatial AOs x 2 spins), 10 electrons. JK_FROZEN_PAIRS 1 freezes
# the 2 LOWEST-energy spin-orbitals (the O 1s core, essentially) at EXACTLY occupation 1 -- never
# an SQP variable. JK_ACTIVE_PAIRS 5 makes the NEXT 10 spin-orbitals by energy the fractional-
# occupation window (sum(n) = NELEC - 2*JK_FROZEN_PAIRS = 8, strictly inside (0, 10) as the SQP's
# box needs); the remaining 14 - 2 - 10 = 2 spin-orbitals (the highest-energy virtuals) are pinned
# at EXACTLY 0 (deep virtual, excluded from the SQP entirely) -- mirroring PNOF's own
# core/active/deep-virtual split (see PNOF_SUBSPACES/PNOF_COUPLING).
NELEC 10
BASIS water-sto-3g.gbs
NON_RELATIVISTIC TRUE
FUNCTIONAL MULLER
JK_FROZEN_PAIRS 1
JK_ACTIVE_PAIRS 5

GEOMETRY
O   0.000000   0.000000   0.000000
H   0.000000   0.757000   0.586000
H   0.000000  -0.757000   0.586000
END
